---
import Base from '@brandon_m_behring/book-scaffold-astro/layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="AI Engineering Guides" description="Company-agnostic, interview-prep-led guides on the AI-native dimensions of AI engineering — evaluation, LLM application engineering, production, craft, and working with AI. Part of guides.brandon-behring.dev.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>The AI-native dimensions of AI engineering</h1>
    <p>
      Company-agnostic, interview-prep-led guides for engineers moving into
      AI-native roles. Organized by what AI-engineering interviews actually test
      and the documented reasons strong candidates fail — taught for transfer to
      the novel problems real interviews throw at you, not memorization.
    </p>

    <h2>Guides</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong><a href="/ai-engineering/chapters/evaluation/why-evaluation/">Evaluation &amp; benchmarking</a></strong>
        — arguably the scarce skill of 2025–26 as model training commoditizes:
        deciding what &ldquo;good&rdquo; means for a real system, measuring it
        honestly, and knowing how the measurement itself can lie.
        <em>Complete — 13 chapters.</em>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong><a href="/ai-engineering/chapters/llm-app-engineering/why-llm-app-engineering/">LLM application engineering</a></strong>
        — building reliable systems on top of models: prompting as a discipline,
        retrieval &amp; RAG, agents and tool use, and the cost/latency trade-offs
        that decide a design. <em>In progress.</em>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      Each guide is paired with a hand-rolled <code>companion</code> library you
      build chapter-by-chapter (<code>mini_eval</code> for evaluation,
      <code>mini_rag</code> for retrieval) — deliberately minimal and
      <em>for learning, not production</em> — then bridge to the production tools
      (<code>eval-toolkit</code>, RAGAS).
    </p>
    <p>
      Part of the <a href="https://guides.brandon-behring.dev/">guides.brandon-behring.dev</a> hub.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
